<title>USA: Fed seen refraining from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed seen refraining from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve is expected to refrain from open market operations on Friday, market analysts said.</p>
<p>Analysts from MCM MoneyWatch, MMS International and Stone &amp; McCarthy Research Associates Inc were all calling for no Fed action.</p>
<p>At 1000 EDT/1400 GMT, federal funds were trading at 5-1/8 percent, below the central bank's 5-1/4 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
